Thus overall plan steps:

Phase A: Prepare origin_availability_alpha.
Phase B: Prepare destination_availability_alpha.
Phase C: Assemble transport leg and authorize loading.
Phase D: Dispatch shift_candidate_alpha to free vehicle_unit_gamma and dispatch slot.
Phase E: Prepare shift_candidate_beta (allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm preparedness, assign operator, assign skill certificate, release compliance from alpha, assign compliance to beta).
Phase F: Load container onto leg (requires shift_candidate_beta prepared etc).
Phase G: Stage shift_candidate_beta.
Phase H: Verify loading profile nominal.
Phase I: Establish clearance nominal.
Phase J: Attach service window.
Phase K: Validate route sequence.
Phase L: Finalize shift_candidate_beta (via sequence validation) -> candidate_finalized, dispatch_ready.
Phase M: Allocate dispatch slot for origin_availability_alpha.
